these programs that we find around and

01:00:09.491 --> 01:00:14.210
we're going to try to empirically
figure out how often we

01:00:14.210 --> 01:00:19.050
can make a big improvement over
what the compilers do now.

01:00:19.050 --> 01:00:23.878
So I'm looking for volunteers for
this summer project.

01:00:23.878 --> 01:00:27.378
Okay, now, how are we doing on time?

01:00:27.378 --> 01:00:30.836
Okay, good.

01:00:30.836 --> 01:00:38.086
I, then I guess it would be time for
me now to say what's the take away?

01:00:38.086 --> 01:00:43.021
Except in 1969,
I wouldn't have said that because

01:00:43.021 --> 01:00:48.586
that's a modern phrase but anyway,
what do we get out of this?

01:00:48.586 --> 01:00:53.604
First of all I wanted to
show you that by trying to

01:00:53.604 --> 01:00:58.373
use mathematics to find
quantitative things

01:00:58.373 --> 01:01:03.517
about computer programs
we add a new dimension to

01:01:03.517 --> 01:01:09.120
what we thought we knew
before about a program.

01:01:09.120 --> 01:01:13.440
Secondly I wanted to show
you that the techniques are,

01:01:13.440 --> 01:01:16.400
they have some kind of a system to them.

01:01:16.400 --> 01:01:17.680
They feed on each other.

01:01:17.680 --> 01:01:22.290
You can, each program doesn't
have its own special trick.

01:01:22.290 --> 01:01:27.119
But these things,
it turns out that there's,

01:01:27.119 --> 01:01:31.836
that we begin to learn
the discrete calculus.

01:01:31.836 --> 01:01:36.548
That that was analogous to the infinite

01:01:36.548 --> 01:01:41.260
calculus that we've been taught, and

01:01:41.260 --> 01:01:46.114
I wanted to show you that it's enjoyable

01:01:46.114 --> 01:01:50.539
to psyche out these problems, and so

01:01:50.539 --> 01:01:58.818
I believe then that I can safely say
that I've got more than enough for

01:01:58.818 --> 01:02:04.387
one lifetime's career
ahead of me of pleasant

01:02:04.387 --> 01:02:10.817
applications that combine
traditional mathematics

01:02:10.817 --> 01:02:15.876
with efficient use of computers, okay?

01:02:15.876 --> 01:02:17.461
Thanks a lot for listening.
[LAUGH]

